{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775332043-tMbPUe3zghZKaLL55PZB","role":"assistant","created":1775332080,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the data I need. Let me extract the Judicial Branch outlays from FY 2007 to FY 2013.\n\nFrom the 2011 bulletin:\n- 2007: 6008\n- 2008: 6345\n- 2009: 6643\n- 2010: 7185\n- 2011: 7296\n\nFrom the 2014 bulletin:\n- 2010: 7185 (matches)\n- 2011: 7295 (slightly different from 7296 - likely rounding)\n- 2012: 7228\n- 2013: 7066\n\nSo for FY 2007-2013:\n- 2007: 6008\n- 2008: 6345\n- 2009: 6643\n- 2010: 7185\n- 2011: 7296 (using 2011 bulletin value)\n- 2012: 7228\n- 2013: 7066\n\nNow I need to calculate the YoY growth rates and then run an OLS regression of ln(outlays) on fiscal year index.\n\nLet me use Python to do the calculations.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_ac92c2a60b9f4775a6488556","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Judicial Branch outlays (in millions) from FY 2007-2013\noutlays = {\n    2007: 6008,\n    2008: 6345,\n    2009: 6643,\n    2010: 7185,\n    2011: 7296,  # using value from 2011 bulletin\n    2012: 7228,\n    2013: 7066\n}\n\n# Year-over-Year growth rates\nyears = sorted(outlays.keys())\nyoy_growth = []\nfor i in range(1, len(years)):\n    prev_year = years[i-1]\n    curr_year = years[i]\n    growth = (outlays[curr_year] - outlays[prev_year]) / outlays[prev_year] * 100\n    yoy_growth.append(growth)\n    print(f\"YoY Growth {prev_year}->{curr_year}: {outlays[prev_year]} -> {outlays[curr_year]} = {growth:.4f}%\")\n\n# Average YoY growth rate\navg_yoy = np.mean(yoy_growth)\nprint(f\"\\nAverage YoY Growth Rate: {avg_yoy:.4f}%\")\n\n# OLS regression of ln(outlays) on fiscal year index\n# Using fiscal year index: 2007=0, 2008=1, ..., 2013=6\ny = np.array([np.log(outlays[y]) for y in years])\nx = np.array([i for i in range(len(years))])\n\n# OLS: y = alpha + beta*x\n# beta = cov(x,y)/var(x)\n# alpha = mean(y) - beta*mean(x)\nx_mean = np.mean(x)\ny_mean = np.mean(y)\nbeta = np.sum((x - x_mean) * (y - y_mean)) / np.sum((x - x_mean)**2)\nalpha = y_mean - beta * x_mean\n\nprint(f\"\\nOLS Regression: ln(outlays) = {alpha:.6f} + {beta:.6f} * year_index\")\nprint(f\"Slope (beta): {beta:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Intercept (alpha): {alpha:.6f}\")\n\n# Round to nearest thousandth as requested\nprint(f\"\\nFinal values (rounded to thousandth):\")\nprint(f\"Average YoY Growth Rate: {round(avg_yoy, 3)}%\")\nprint(f\"OLS Slope: {round(beta, 3)}\")\nprint(f\"OLS Intercept: {round(alpha, 3)}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
